# IT-Inventory Deployment Walkthrough (Bypass Strategy)

We have successfully bypassed the ZimaOS infrastructure restrictions that were blocking Git/SSH operations in Coolify V4.

## Changes Made

### [Component] File Synchronization
- All project files from `c:\projects\it-inventory` were synced directly to the DeanOS server via SSH at `/DATA/AppData/it-inventory`.
- File extraction permissions were handled, ensuring all critical files (`Dockerfile`, `main.py`, etc.) are ready.

### [Component] Coolify V4 Configuration
- **Old Strategy:** Abandoned Git/SSH due to ZimaOS kernel restrictions.
- **New Strategy:** Direct Docker-Compose deployment aiming at the local file system.
- **Result:** Successfully bypassed 'Read-only file system' errors.

## Verification Results

### Manual Verification
- [x] Files successfully landed on server: `ls -la /DATA/AppData/it-inventory` confirmed.
- [x] Correct Port mapping configured: `9700 (Host) -> 8000 (Container)`.
- [x] Database persistence setup at `/DATA/AppData/it-inventory/data`.

